 {:seon.task/name "a-prefixed-collection-indents-its-members-past-its-opener"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the printer audit (notes/archive/printer-audit-2026-10-25.md). A namespace-lifted map prints `#:seon.task{:kind :work,` and its later keys under the `#`, eleven columns left of `:kind`, so they read as the parent's (every agent's context shows its task so); `#error {:via` does the same. Cause: ```seon.print.emit/emit-collection``` nests a map's members one column past the group's indentation, not past its opener, and ```seon.print.select/member-indent``` charges that same one column, not knowing the lift. Correct: members nest past the opener (`#:seon.task{` is 12 columns) and the selection charges what the emitter lays out, its lift decided once where both read it. Proof: a lifted map of three keys under a narrow width prints each key in one column, inside its charge (seon.print-test/the-text-stays-inside-its-budget stays green)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.print-test/a-lifted-map-indents-its-keys-past-its-opener}}
 {:seon.task/name "breadth-shows-no-member-that-shows-nothing"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the printer audit (notes/archive/printer-audit-2026-10-25.md; owner, 2026-10-25: elision placeholders should not be printed). ```seon.print.select/fill-rows``` shows rows whole then one cut, but a collection of rows with one member of another kind falls back to ```seon.print.select/fill-members```, which places every member at its least first: 177 rows and a keyword print 177 lines of `{…7 (get-in result/e1 [N])}`. Correct: breadth places a member whose least form shows nothing only where a later member that shows something needs its position; a run of them at the tail is the collection's one cut. Proof: (assoc rows 3 :odd) of 177 rows prints no `{…` line and one cut past the rows shown."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.print-test/breadth-shows-no-member-that-shows-nothing}}]
